Contact Management System

A Contact Management System developed in C++ using a Binary Search Tree (BST) to efficiently organize and manage contact information.

Overview

This project was developed to apply fundamental Data Structures and Algorithms concepts to a practical application. Contacts are organized in the Binary Search Tree based on the contact name, allowing alphabetical traversal and efficient name-based searching.

The system provides essential functionality for adding, searching, editing, deleting, and managing contacts.

Features
Add new contacts
Search contacts by name
Search contacts by phone number
Edit existing contact details
Delete contacts
Mark or unmark contacts as favourites
Display all contacts alphabetically
Display favourite contacts
Prevent duplicate phone numbers
Validate Gmail addresses
Load contacts from a file
Save contacts to a file
Contact Information

Each contact contains:

Name
Phone Number
Email
Address
Favourite Status
Data Structure Used
Binary Search Tree

The system uses a Binary Search Tree, with the contact's name serving as the key.

              Rahul
             /     \
        Arjun       Vijay
        /   \         \
     Anand  Ravi      Zoya

Contacts are arranged according to alphabetical order.

An inorder traversal of the BST produces contacts in alphabetical order.

Operations
Insertion

New contacts are inserted according to their names while maintaining the BST property.

Searching
Name-based searching utilizes the BST structure.
Phone-number searching traverses the tree because the BST is ordered by name.
Deletion

The system handles all three standard BST deletion cases:

Node with no children
Node with one child
Node with two children
File Handling

Contact information is stored in contacts.txt, allowing the data to be loaded when the program starts and saved when the program exits.

